      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "=====",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "MAYBE Move StroikaConfig to IntermediateFiles/CONFIGURATIONAMME folder?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tRedo WINDOWS build scripts so they take a TARGET CONFIGUARION as arg. And just build that one at a time. This will better mimic what we do for unix, will allow the getnic build to just do one or two configs,a nd allow external specification of the set of configs to build (so you CAN build the “A” builds quickly – just to test).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tSimilarly – do for RUNTESTS code – takes arg of configuarion.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tALSO – have MAKE CONFIGUARION=XXX build configuration XXX, but make with no CONFIGUARTION= value internally iterate over ALL configuarionts calling MAKE (with same commandline args – $(TARGETOGALS? Or (COMMANDLINEAR?GS???S) but adding CONFIGUARTION=X for each configuration.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
